      "closure_rationale": "The real retained TLV admits known-number/empty and advisory unknown bytes while rejecting malformed known forms and unsupported critical tags. The owned record narrows each payload to16 bytes, admits0..8 fields, rejects known duplicates and preserves every unknown occurrence. Whole admission through actual FCursor/f_take and retained ADT TLV parsing precedes publication. Byte bounds and disjoint borrowed/owned lifetimes are explicit: original single-TLV retains255-byte support and borrowed mutation behavior; new owned copies do not change after source mutation. Actual ar_encode/ar_decode format1/2 records relay opaquely through tag3. Source comparison distinguishes Protobuf retention from its duplicate/field-order policy and from this original canonical format. Six compiler profiles compare10100 independent grammar/stable-order/HMAC/state cases,5244 admitted, against full buffer/tag/service outputs. Truncation, trailing input, all selected capacities, zero-length unknowns, maximum145-byte records and maximum255-byte original TLVs are exercised. Eight compiled controls per profile reject normally, including both retained defects; four compiling learner anchors fail. Compiler closures bind actual cursor, codec and first-principles HMAC providers. Stable tag ordering preserves equal-tag duplicate order and authenticates every occurrence with an exact versioned/domain-separated HMAC transcript. An original local projection defect admits tag9 duplicate edits and increments only a synthetic privileged counter; complete-transcript verification rejects the old code, and a separate whitelist refuses even freshly authenticated unknown semantics. Counter overflow leaves both fields unchanged. Signature transcript participation is specified without claiming asymmetric execution. The delayed ordering/version/policy variant, thirteen cost rows and repeated maximum-record measurements are supplied. Bounded author support; no unaided delayed learner result or non-author assessment inferred."
    },
